# Post-push production chat status (for the site owner in Cursor)

This is **not** the in-app customer toast. Tell **you** in this chat whether production chat is up after commits that affect production or when you pushed in the task.

## Steps

1. Run `node scripts/chat-production-status.mjs` (instant; the script never waits unless `CHAT_HEALTH_ALLOW_LONG_WAIT=1`). Do not set wait env vars for normal agent checks.
2. If the script exits non-zero or prints `Status: Chat Offline`, note what failed briefly.
3. The **last line** of your reply after a push (or when the task included push) must be exactly one of:
   - `**Production chat:** Online`
   - `**Production chat:** Offline` (plus one short sentence on what failed)

Do not run a multi-minute wait before the script. Default script wait is zero.

## When to skip

- Question-only or review-only tasks with no push.
- User explicitly says not to report chat status for that task.
- Doc-only or dev-only changes (`/devchat`, Dify dev, planning docs) with no production deploy concern, unless the user asks.

